# Flash Sale Microservice: Architecture & Verification Plan

Before we write a single line of code, here is exactly why the **Flash Sale Engine** is the ultimate proof that Hrux-DB is a production-ready database, and exactly how we will use the external application to test every single feature.

## Why is a Flash Sale the "Best Fit"?
A Flash Sale (e.g., 10,000 people trying to buy 500 iPhones at the exact same second) is the hardest problem in database engineering. 
- **SQL databases fail** because 10,000 queries try to update the exact same `inventory` row, causing a "Row Lock" bottleneck that crashes the server.
- **Pure caches fail** because if the server loses power mid-sale, the financial inventory data is wiped out.
- **Redis bottlenecks** because it processes all 10,000 requests in a single-file line on one CPU core.

By building an external Node.js application that runs a Flash Sale, we prove that **Hrux-DB solves all these problems simultaneously.**

