## Feature Testing Matrix (The "Big One")
We will create a separate folder called `microservice-flashsale`. It will use our new `hrux-client.js` SDK to communicate with Hrux-DB. Here is how the microservice will explicitly prove **every single feature** of Hrux-DB:

| Hrux-DB Feature | How the Microservice Tests & Proves It |
| :--- | :--- |
| **1. In-Memory Speed** | We will show a live throughput graph. Because it's purely in-memory, the graph will show Hrux-DB effortlessly handling thousands of operations per second with microsecond latency, dwarfing SQL's capabilities. |
| **2. Concurrency (Sharding)** | We will write a "Load Test Script" that blasts the microservice with thousands of parallel `/buy` requests. Hrux-DB will route these across its 256 shards, utilizing your entire CPU without locking up. |
| **3. Crash Recovery** | During the live load test, we will physically kill the Hrux-DB server (`Ctrl+C`). When we restart it, the microservice will immediately resume, proving the inventory count didn't lose a single item. |
| **4. Durability (WAL)** | The master `inventory_count` is what guarantees crash recovery. We will show the `.wal` file actively growing as purchases happen. |
| **5. Auto-Compaction** | As the load test hits 100,000 operations, we will watch the massive WAL file automatically shrink itself into a clean snapshot without interrupting the sale! |
| **6. Real-Time (Pub/Sub)** | Every time an item is successfully purchased, the microservice calls `db.publish()`. A Live Admin Dashboard will subscribe to this and show a real-time scrolling feed of purchases. |
| **7. TTL (Time-To-Live)** | When a user clicks "Add to Cart", the microservice stores a `cart_reservation` key with a **300-second TTL**. If they don't buy in 5 minutes, Hrux-DB auto-deletes the reservation and frees up inventory. |
| **8. Sets (Unique Data)** | We use a Hrux-DB `Set` to store `buyer_ids`. This guarantees that even if a user's browser glitches and sends 50 duplicate requests, they can only buy the item once. |
| **9. Queues (Waitlists)** | Once inventory hits 0, users who try to buy are automatically `pushed` onto a Hrux-DB `Queue` to form a perfectly ordered Waitlist. |
| **10. Safe Iteration (SCAN)** | The Admin Dashboard will use the `SCAN` command to safely scroll through the list of active cart sessions without freezing the database. |

